        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on current pain points and approve target tax workflow scope.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 109659,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hello team, welcome to the official channel for the Tax Workflow Standardisation project. The main goal is to create a more robust and uniform process for everyone. To start, let's define the scope. I suggest we focus initially on the core data collection from Finance, Operations, and Sales, as this is where most delays seem to happen. What are your thoughts? I've opened up T1 to begin mapping the current state.",
            "mentions": [
              27135,
              60334,
              66260,
              543897
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 60334,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Thanks for kicking this off! Agree with that focus. Operations is definitely a key area, their data handover is always different. Should we also include Marketing's promotional expense reports? They are often a source of confusion for tax deductions.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 66260,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "From a tax perspective, the main issue is inconsistent invoice summaries from Sales. We spend days re-formatting them. So yes, Sales must be in scope.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_plus_sign",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 109659,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Good point on Marketing. Let's add them to the initial scope for T1 mapping. We can scale back later if it becomes too complex, but it's better to have the data upfront.",
            "mentions": [
              60334
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 543897,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Sounds good. So the scope is Finance, Operations, Sales, and Marketing. That seems manageable for the first pass.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
